.TH DAYBOOK 1 "November 2026" "Daybook @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daybook \- personal work planner with a daily plan, timer and reminders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daybook
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fITEXT\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Daybook plans the working day around meetings, tracks time with a focus timer, and sends
reminders. All data is stored in one SQLite file, \fI~/.local/share/daybook/daybook.db\fR.
.PP
A second invocation is handed to the Daybook that is already running, so every option below
works from a terminal, a launcher or a keyboard shortcut.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-quick\-add
Open Quick Add. Any \fITEXT\fR after it is filled in.
.TP
.B \-\-meeting\-now
Start an unplanned meeting.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without a window, so reminders still arrive. Used by "Start at login".
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print one line about the running timer and exit. Works when Daybook is not running.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Also write log messages to the terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAYBOOK_DATA_DIR
Use another data folder (a throwaway database).
.TP
.B DAYBOOK_FAKE_NOW, DAYBOOK_TIME_SCALE
Fake and speed up the clock, for testing reminders. Only with DAYBOOK_DATA_DIR set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/daybook/daybook.db
The database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/daybook/backups/
Daily backups (the last 14).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/daybook/daybook.log
The log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/io.github.daybook.Daybook.desktop
Created by "Start at login".
